  "body": "### What are you trying to do\n\nA desired tool path type/output would be Peck Threading, where during the threading operation the tool will pull out of the cut a very tiny bit and then reengage to prevent long stringy chips in materials that are hard to form chips such as stainless steels and heat resistant super alloys.\n\n### How you imagine it working\n\nAs part of the threading cycle (if supported by the controller) or as a raw point to point out put, the tool would move out of the cut by the depth of cut to break the chip. It should then do a spring pass at that depth to clean up the previous pass and get those couple of highspots to prevent a sudden spike in chip load on the pass at the next depth.",
